  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Solve each of the following quadratic equations by first putting each into standard form:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-3x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{13}}2$",
          "worked": "$$x^2-3x-1=0.$$\n$a=1$, $b=-3$, $c=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-3)\\pm\\sqrt{(-3)^2-4(1)(-1)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{13}}2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x-2)^2=3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{7\\pm\\sqrt{33}}2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x+4&=3x\\\\x^2-7x+4&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$a=1$, $b=-7$, $c=4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-7)\\pm\\sqrt{(-7)^2-4(1)(4)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{7\\pm\\sqrt{33}}2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac3x+2=4x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{13}}4$\n\nMultiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3+2x&=4x^2\\\\4x^2-2x-3&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$a=4$, $b=-2$, $c=-3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(4)(-3)}}{2(4)}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{52}}8\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{13}}4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots satisfy $x\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(x+1)^2=3x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+2x+1&=3x+2\\\\x^2-x-1&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$a=1$, $b=-1$, $c=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-1)\\pm\\sqrt{(-1)^2-4(1)(-1)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x+3)^2+x^2-8=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt7}2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+6x+9+x^2-8&=0\\\\2x^2+6x+1&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$a=2$, $b=6$, $c=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{6^2-4(2)(1)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{28}}4\\\\x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt7}2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1x+\\frac1{x+1}=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}2$\n\nMultiply by $x(x+1)$, then use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0,-1$. Multiply by $x(x+1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)+x&=x(x+1)\\\\2x+1&=x^2+x\\\\x^2-x-1&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$a=1$, $b=-1$, $c=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-1)\\pm\\sqrt{(-1)^2-4(1)(-1)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}2\\end{align*}$$\nNeither root is $0$ or $-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
